! mcp_bootstrap_p194.strap -- MCP printed page 194: the index-register
! save area of the new-tape routine, and J WRITL, the "analysis of I/O
! indicators for WRITE LABEL" routine -- the EPGK/unload arm, the
! operator "put a ring in reel" message, the read-label-back-and-
! compare arm, and the JRWRIT rewrite-label entry.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_001-249.pdf PDF p.201.  The header was READ at 600
! dpi, not assumed:  "TIME CLOCK 00054041   PUNID 11D11MCP   CARD ID
! LG000267   DIST. OF 3/01   3/01   PAGE NUMBER  194".
!
! >>> THE COLUMN-HEADING ROW'S OWN "LOCATION" FIELD READS 221617. <<<
! Read at 600 dpi, six digits, well clear of the dashed rule
! (<SCRATCHPAD>/hdloc-201.png).  By docs/transcription_workflow.md
! step 1 that is LINE 1'S location, and line 1 here IS a located row,
! which is the case the rule predicts to be NUMBERED rather than
! blank.  Line 1's own LOCATION column reads 221617.00 at 1600 dpi.
! Two independent witnesses for the origin, and a third below.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT THE PAGE IS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FIFTY PRINTED LINES.  FORTY-THREE COMPILE; SEVEN ARE COMMENT
! CARDS (lines 2-7 and line 40, printed "--" in the NAME column).
! No SLC, no CNOP, no DD.  ONE RESERVATION -- line 1's
! "DRZ(N),(3)" -- and it plants THREE WORDS OF ZEROS rather than
! leaving a hole, so the page is CONTIGUOUS from 221617.00 to
! 221651.77 with nothing skipped.
!
!   line  1       JNEWXR, the three-word index-register save area
!                 that printed p.192 line 51's "JNEWTE
!                 TI,3,$1,JNEWXR" transmits into.  Its defining
!                 card is on THIS page; see THE DRZ, below.
!   lines  2-7    the banner "*****ANALYSIS OF I/O INDICATORS FOR
!                 WRITE LABEL*****" and the linkage comment
!                 "LINKAGE....SIC,JWRITX...B,JWRITL".
!   lines  8-13   J WRITL itself: save three index registers into
!                 JPREVX, SIC/B into KCONVR/KCONV to set up the
!                 channel and unit number, a VF holding JINSCU
!                 (the bit address the converted unit number is
!                 inserted at), then two BB's on S IO IND bits 9
!                 and 10 -- EPGK to JEPGKF, the next bit to
!                 JRWRIT.
!   lines 14-25   JEPGKF, the file-protect arm: unload the unit
!                 (LX,$0,JUNLDK + the standard SIC,KKRET /
!                 B,KIOREJ / LVI,$1,$+1.0 / B,JSEOPT / NOP / NOP
!                 I-O sequence), loop back to JEPGKF, then
!                 SIC,SCOMIC / B,SCOMM with two parameter half
!                 words -- ",JINSM" (the message) and ",8.0" (its
!                 length) -- to tell the operator to put a ring in
!                 the reel.
!   lines 26-39   JUNRL waits for the unit to become ready
!                 (SIC,KUNRR / B,KKLOOP), sets the read-label
!                 tally (LCI,$3,3), and JRDLAB reads the label
!                 back and compares it: LF(BU,30),JLABIN against
!                 KF(BU,30),SSCRPM($12), BZAE to JBDLAB if the
!                 labels differ.
!   line  40      "***** ENTER HERE IF ONLY WRITE LABEL REQUIRED
!                 *****"
!   lines 41-50   JRWRIT: reset the tally, JBACKT backspaces the
!                 tape (SIC,JBSPX / B,JBSPE), JTRYLG erases a long
!                 gap (LX,$0,JERGK) and runs the same six-card I-O
!                 sequence.  The page ends mid-routine; printed
!                 p.195 line 1 is "B,JTRYLG".
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE SPAN, ESTABLISHED FROM THE PAGE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The brief no longer quotes survey endpoints and this deck did not
! consult them.  Four readings, and they agree:
!
!   * THE HEADING'S OWN LOCATION FIELD: 221617.
!   * THE LINE COLUMN runs 1..50 with no break.  Line 1 is located
!     (221617.00) and line 50 is located (221651.00); below line 50
!     there is nothing but the closing dashed rule.
!   * THE CARD-SERIAL COLUMN runs LG000267 (line 1; the heading's
!     own CARD ID says LG000267 too) to LG000316 (line 50) -- FIFTY
!     serials for FIFTY lines, consecutive, no duplicate and no
!     gap.  Nothing fell off either end.
!     >>> BUT LG000317 PRINTS NO LINE ANYWHERE. <<<  printed p.195
!     line 1 carries LG000318, read at 600 dpi, and p.194 line 50
!     carries LG000316, also read at 600 dpi.  That is a third
!     instance of the workflow's "a serial that prints NO listing
!     line does occur, both at page breaks" (ED000049, IH000041).
!     It is a PAGE BREAK again, so the pattern holds; it is not a
!     lost row of THIS page, because this page's counter closes
!     without slack (below).
!     A SECOND GAP MAY SIT AT THE p.192/p.193 BREAK -- printed
!     p.193's heading CARD ID is LG000215 against p.192's last
!     LISTING LINE LG000213 -- but I am NOT generalizing from it
!     and nobody should.  Those are different quantities (a
!     heading field against a line's serial), p.192 is recorded as
!     carrying a DUPLICATE serial on two of its lines, and two
!     observations are not a rule.  The brief's example of exactly
!     this mistake is printed p.147 proposing a rule its own
!     afternoon refuted.  So: ONE gap measured at 600 dpi on both
!     sides (LG000316 / LG000318), mechanism unknown, no rule
!     proposed.
!   * THE COUNTER CHAIN closes digit for digit.  3 reserved words +
!     5 full-word instructions (lines 8, 12, 13, 37, 38) + 37
!     half-word instructions + line 11's VF (25 bits, rounded to
!     the half word) = 26.5 words, and 0o221617 + 0o32 = 0o221651,
!     so the page runs 221617.00 .. 221651.77 and the next card
!     falls at 221651.40.
!
! >>> THE FORWARD JOIN IS A PRINTED WITNESS, NOT ARITHMETIC. <<<
! printed p.195 line 1 reads, at 600 dpi:
!
!     1*  221651.40   221646.10 00        B,JTRYLG
!
! which is this page's predicted next location EXACTLY, and whose
! operand is a label THIS page defines (JTRYLG, line 44, 221646.00;
! 0o00 OR 0o10 = 0o10).  So the tail is checked twice over.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE DRZ -- THE THING THE CALLER ASKED TO BE READ OFF THE INK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! printed p.192's deck note (5) recorded that a later page's OCR
! carried JNEWXR's defining card as "221617.00  000003.60 ...
! JNEWXR  DRZ(..),(3)".  That page is THIS one, and the ink says:
!
!     1*  221617.00  *   000003.00        JNEWXR   DRZ(N),(3)
!
! read at 1600 dpi for the binary and 1200 dpi for the statement
! (<SCRATCHPAD>/l1_bin-201.png, <SCRATCHPAD>/l1_stmt-201.png).
!
!   * THE COUNT IS 000003.00, NOT 000003.60.  The OCR's ".60" is
!     wrong; the two octal digits are a clean 00 at 1600 dpi, and
!     the arithmetic agrees -- three words from 221617 puts line 8
!     at 221622.00, which is what line 8 prints.
!   * THE Z IS THERE.  D, R, Z, unambiguous at 1200 dpi.  This
!     matters exactly as the workflow says it does: a reservation
!     prints its COUNT, so DR and DRZ are indistinguishable to
!     every !CHECK on the page, and the difference is three words
!     of zero content in the merged image.  It is read off the ink
!     and it can never be read off a passing run.
!   * MODE "(N)" IS NORMALIZED FLOATING POINT.  C22-6531's "Data
!     Description" section: "There are seven fixed use mode
!     designators: 1. N Normalized Floating Point / 2. U
!     Unnormalized Floating Point / 3. B Binary / 4. BU Binary
!     Unsigned / 5. D Decimal ..." -- so N is a use mode of exactly
!     the same kind as the BU these decks write everywhere, not a
!     misread letter.  C28-6129 repeats it ("N Normalized Floating
!     Point") and adds "Use mode N should have no entry mode",
!     which is why no entry-mode prefix is printed beside it.  Its
!     unit is a 64-bit floating word, and the counter confirms
!     that here: three N's take exactly three words.
!     (strap_asm's MODE_BITS carries only B/BU/D/DU, which are the
!     VFL modes; "(N)" on a RESERVATION never reaches that table,
!     so the card assembles and the count is right.  A VFL
!     operation written "(N)" would be a different question and
!     this page does not ask it.)
!   * IT DOES NOT SETTLE THE BRIEF'S OPEN "(BU)"-INHERITANCE
!     QUESTION.  "(N)" here is mode-only, but it is on a
!     RESERVATION with no operand symbol to inherit a length FROM,
!     so this row says nothing about whether a mode-only dds
!     inherits from its operand.
!
! A SECOND INSTANCE OF THE SAME CARD IS ON printed p.195, and its
! OCR is legible: "45# 221730.00 # COCCO3.CC , JPREVX DRZ(N),(3)
! -FOR INDEX REGISTERS".  Same shape, same count, same mode, and
! its comment says what the three words are for -- the three index
! registers a "TI,3,$1,X" transmits.  (That OCR is of a DIFFERENT
! page, so it is an index to where JPREVX is defined; it is not
! offered as corroboration of p.194's own ink.)
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! GLYPH CALLS -- the round glyphs, each with how it was settled
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! (1) LINE 36 "B,JERRD" and LINE 39 "BZAE,JBDLAB": BOTH END IN A
!     D, NOT AN O, AND THE VOLUME OCR SAYS OTHERWISE.  Settled on
!     the workflow's left-side discriminator -- "C and 0 are round
!     with no stem; D has a straight vertical left stem and squared
!     corners" -- at 1600 dpi, with a KNOWN C in the SAME ROW for
!     contrast:
!
!       p.194 l.36  "B,JERRD"            final glyph: straight left stem
!       p.195 l.16  "JERRD  SIC,JBSPX"   same, against the round C of SIC
!       p.194 l.39  "BZAE,JBDLAB"        straight left stem
!       p.195 l.22  "JBDLAB LV,$2,SCREEL($12)"  same, against SCREEL's C
!       p.195 l.19  "CB,$3,JRDLAB"       the C of CB and the D of JRDLAB
!                                        in one row, visibly different
!
!     The last of those is the decisive one: one row, one drum, a C
!     and the disputed glyph side by side.
!     THE VOLUME OCR READS THESE WRONG AND SAYS SO LOUDLY: a
!     whole-name census over both volumes returns JRD* ZERO times
!     (it reads JRDLAB as "JRCLAB" and JRDLK as "JROLK"), while
!     giving "JERRO" once.  A reader that never once gets a D right
!     in this symbol family is not a witness against a D.
!     Semantics agree on every one: JRDLAB = ReaD LABel (its own
!     comment is "-READ LABEL"), JBDLAB = BaD LABel (reached from
!     "-IF NOT SAME LABEL"), JERRD on the error path.
!
!     >>> BUT BE HONEST ABOUT WHAT THIS IS: IT IS SHAPE, APPLIED
!     >>> TWICE. <<<  The workflow's own measurement says every
!     round glyph settled in this corpus was settled "by another
!     page, a manual, or the compiled word -- never by shape", and
!     the left-stem discriminator IS shape.  What raises it above a
!     guess here is (a) the same-row C/D contrast, which holds
!     position, row, drum and ink fixed, (b) JRDLAB being anchored
!     by its own English comment, and (c) the OCR's demonstrated
!     inability to read a D in this family at all.  It is not a
!     manual and it is not a compiled word.
!     NOTHING DOWNSTREAM CAN CATCH IT: no landed deck references
!     JERRD or JBDLAB, so the merge is silent and these two rest on
!     ink alone -- the exact case the workflow says to re-read at
!     1800 dpi.  BOTH DEFINING CARDS ARE ON printed p.195
!     (221661.40 and 221664.40), so that page's transcriber owns
!     the decisive reading and should take it: if either comes back
!     an O, this deck's SYN name is wrong (its VALUE is not, since
!     the branch bytes check the address).
!
! (2) LINE 1 "DRZ(N)": the N is unambiguous at 1200 dpi and is a
!     real STRAP use mode (above).
!
! (3) "SIOIND" (lines 12, 13): the final glyph is a D, matching the
!     landed "SIOIND SYN(BU,5), 1.09" in SEVEN decks and the
!     typeset C22-6728 (2 hits in each revision).  Printed with NO
!     blanks, unlike the "S IO IND" form other pages print.
!
! (4) "KCONVR"/"KCONV" (lines 9, 10): both round glyphs are round
!     with no stem; the landed spelling in four and three decks
!     respectively.
!
! (5) "JINSCU" (line 11): round, no stem, so C not D.  The name is
!     ALSO carried by printed p.195's OCR against its defining card
!     at the very bit address this row compiles -- "22% 221704.20 ,
!     JINSCU (1QS*)OC(BU),XX UNIT X AND READY THE UNIT." -- a
!     different page, so a genuine index.  The comment column two
!     rows up ("-SET UP CHANNEL AND / -UNIT NO.") says what it is:
!     the field the converted Channel/Unit number is inserted into.
!
! (6) LINE 39's comment prints "-IF NOT SZME LABEL".  The word is
!     SAME; the A prints as a Z.  Recorded, not corrected, and it
!     is a comment so nothing depends on it.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE LOCATION-COLUMN ASTERISK
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THREE rows carry the second asterisk, after the location:
!
!     line  1   221617.00 *     JNEWXR  DRZ(N),(3)
!     line 27   221635.00 *     B,KKLOOP
!     line 49   221650.40 *     NOP
!
! Recorded and no rule proposed, per the brief.  They are a
! reservation, a branch and a NOP; they have no operation, no
! operand form, no name-field state and no serial pattern in
! common (LG000267, LG000293, LG000315), and lines 19/20/34/35/50
! are NOPs that do NOT carry it, which kills "every NOP" from
! inside this one page.  The ninth thing it is not.
!
! (Note that EVERY line number on this page is followed by an
! asterisk in the LINE column -- "1*", "2*", ... "50*".  That is
! the column separator, not the mark; the mark is the SECOND
! asterisk, to the right of the location.)
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! EXTERNALS, AND WHAT EACH ROW ACTUALLY READS OF THEM
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! Measured through strap_asm rather than assumed (the sweep in
! docs/transcription_workflow.md "WHAT THE ORACLE CANNOT SEE" 1):
!
!   BIT-EXACT -- the row is a READING of the whole 24-bit address:
!     SIC rows        KCONVR KKRET SCOMIC KUNRR JBSPX
!     VFL operands    JLABIN (LF), SSCRPM (KF)
!     line 11's VF    JINSCU
!     lines 24/25's blank-operation half words   JINSM
!
!     >>> THE BLANK-OPERATION ROW READS EVERY BIT, AND THAT WAS
!     >>> MEASURED, NOT ASSUMED. <<<  ",8.0" compiling 000010.00
!     proves only that the WORD is right, because both operands
!     have bit 0.  Sweeping a SYN through the workflow's five
!     offsets against ",X":
!
!         SYN offset ->  .00        .01        .37        .40        .41
!         ,X:            221701.00  221701.01  221701.37  221701.40  221701.41
!         VF,X:          221704.00  221704.01  221704.37  221704.40  221704.41
!
!     Both are in the VFL/SIC tier: every bit shows.  So JINSM is
!     pinned to 221701.00 AND JINSCU to 221704.20 BY THIS PAGE.
!     (printed p.195's OCR independently carries defining cards at
!     both of those exact bit addresses.)
!
!   HALF WORD ONLY -- a branch or an index operation; the low five
!   bits of these are a CONVENTION and this deck writes ".0":
!     B rows          KCONV KIOREJ JSEOPT SCOMM KKLOOP JERRD JBSPE
!     LX rows         JUNLDK JRDLK JERGK
!     TI 2nd operand  JPREVX
!     BZAE            JBDLAB   (bit 32 SET: the row prints .76)
!
!   Every one of these agrees with its landed value where one
!   exists -- KCONVR 221350.0, KCONV 221335.0, KKRET 221512.40,
!   KIOREJ 221505.0, JSEOPT 221525.0 (printed p.192 DEFINES it),
!   SCOMIC 215470.40, SCOMM 215470.0, KUNRR 221325.40, KKLOOP
!   221321.40, JBSPX 221520.40 (printed p.192 DEFINES it), JBSPE
!   221514.0, SIOIND (BU,5) 1.09, SSCRPM (BU,64) 6.0.
!
!   DATA DESCRIPTIONS CARRIED FROM THE DEFINING PAGE, per the
!   brief: SIOIND takes "(BU,5)" from printed p.102 line 7 and
!   SSCRPM takes "(BU,64)" from printed p.101 line 20.  No page
!   declares a dds for any of the J-symbols above, so none is
!   written for them.
!
!   NOT A SYMBOL OF THIS DECK: "JWRITX", which is named only
!   inside line 6's comment card.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE ORIGIN IS CHECKED, NOT ASSERTED
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! The page prints no SLC, so this deck writes a hard one -- which
! a !CHECK can never contradict.  But THREE LANDED DECKS place
! labels this page DEFINES, all three as hard literals and none as
! a SYN alias (the false positive printed p.189 found):
!
!     printed p.192   JNEWXR  SYN, (8)221617.0     -> line  1
!     printed p.189   JWRITL  SYN, (8)221622.0     -> line  8
!     printed p.190   JRWRIT  SYN, (8)221644.40    -> line 41
!
! THE INJECTION WAS RUN -- not grepped -- against a merge of
! pp.99-192 plus this page (p.193 is in flight and absent):
!
!     origin as printed    MERGE OK (832 defined, 64 external,
!                          2339 words, 0 unaccounted)
!     origin shifted .40   MERGE REFUSED:
!       FAIL JNEWXR: printed p.192 SYNs bit 4776896,
!                    printed p.194 places it at bit 4776960
!
! So the origin is CHECKED, not asserted.  All twenty-seven of this
! page's words (0o221617..0o221651) are present in the merged image
! and the word accounting reports ZERO unaccounted words.
!
! THE ONE OPEN SPAN IN THAT MERGE IS p.193's, and it is this deck's
! forward SLC that covers it: words 0o221542..0o221616, forty-five
! of them, jumped by "SLC,(8)221617.0" because p.193 has not landed.
! That is the brief's warning about a forward SLC keeping the image
! green across a gap it should not be green across.  When p.193
! lands the span closes and the skip disappears; until then nobody
! should read this merge as evidence that pp.193 is accounted for.
!
! A FOURTH WITNESS IS COMING, AND IT IS STRONGER THAN THE THREE
! ABOVE.  printed p.193 line 46 reads, at 600 dpi:
!
!     46*  221613.00   221617.00 80  000021.06 A0   TI,3,JNEWXR,$1
!
! -- the restore of what p.192's "TI,3,$1,JNEWXR" saved.  JNEWXR is
! the FIRST operand there, and a first operand prints its full
! 24-bit bit address (221617.00 80) where p.192's second operand
! printed only 221617.06.  So when p.193 lands it will pin this
! page's line 1 TO THE BIT, which no deck currently does.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! ASSEMBLER: ONE REFUSAL, AND IT IS THE KNOWN ONE
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! All forty-three compiling statements were handed to strap_asm IN
! THEIR PRINTED FORM.  Forty-two were accepted, including
! "DRZ(N),(3)", "VF,JINSCU", the two blank-operation cards
! ",JINSM" and ",8.0", "LF(BU,30),JLABIN" and
! "KF(BU,30),SSCRPM($12)" (which differ only in their second half,
! 036000.06 70 against 036000.23 10, and BOTH reproduce exactly),
! "BZAE,JBDLAB", "BB,SIOIND+.1($13),JRWRIT" and "LCI,$3,3".
!
! THE ONE REFUSAL is the NAME-FIELD BLANK of line 8, which prints
! "J WRITL".  Handed over as printed:
!
!     J WRITL  TI,3,$1,JPREVX
!       -> line 3: unknown mnemonic 'WRITLTI'
!
! which is the brief's known gap ("a blank in the NAME (label)
! field is refused"), not a new finding.  The deck writes JWRITL;
! the printed form is "J WRITL" and the symbol is the same one
! printed p.189 SYNs as JWRITL.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! WHAT WAS RUN, AND ONE MEASUREMENT OF THE TOOLING
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
!   verify_mcp_page.py 194        8 symbols, 42 listing rows, ALL PASSED
!   check_symbol_spellings.py     1596 definitions, no symbol spelled
!                                 two ways (this deck included)
!   check_deck_listing_comments.py  this deck alone: 44 rows parsed,
!                                 42 checks compared, 0 mismatches
!   mcp_image merge + origin injection   see THE ORIGIN, above
!
! >>> check_deck_listing_comments.py COMPARES ONLY THE FIRST EIGHT
! >>> CHARACTERS OF THE BINARY. <<<  Its test is
! `r.startswith(want[:8])`, and `want[:8]` of "221626.50 00" is
! "221626.5".  Measured on this deck by perturbing one listing row
! two ways:
!
!     listing row says 221626.51 00 (!CHECK 221626.50 00) -> PASSES
!     listing row says 221627.50 00 (!CHECK 221626.50 00) -> FAILS
!
! So the self-diff sees the location word and the FIRST octal digit
! of the bit offset, and is blind to the second octal digit and to
! the whole trailing hex byte.  It is still worth running -- it
! caught the second case at once, and it proves it read this deck's
! block -- but "0 mismatches" is a weaker statement than it looks,
! and the brief's "a claim about the REPO" rule says to put the
! measurement here rather than the impression.
!
! ---------------------------------------------------------------

! ----- EXTERNALS ------------------------------------------------
JPREVX  SYN, (8)221730.0             ! line  8 TI 2nd operand prints 221730.06; half word only.
                                     !   printed p.195's OCR carries its defining card,
                                     !   "221730.00 * 000003.00  JPREVX DRZ(N),(3) -FOR INDEX REGISTERS"
KCONVR  SYN, (8)221350.0             ! line  9 SIC -- BIT-EXACT; landed value
KCONV   SYN, (8)221335.0             ! line 10 B prints 221335.10; half word only; landed value
JINSCU  SYN, (8)221704.20            ! line 11 VF -- BIT-EXACT (sweep above).  Bit 0o20 is READ, not convention
SIOIND  SYN(BU,5), 1.09              ! landed p.102 line 7 "-IO INDICATORS"; lines 12/13 print 000001.11 / .12
JUNLDK  SYN, (8)221721.0             ! line 14 LX; half word only.  p.195 OCR defines it at 221721.00
KKRET   SYN, (8)221512.40            ! lines 15/30/45 SIC -- BIT-EXACT; landed value
KIOREJ  SYN, (8)221505.0             ! lines 16/31/46 B; half word only; landed value
JSEOPT  SYN, (8)221525.0             ! lines 18/33/48 B; printed p.192 DEFINES it at 221525.00
SCOMIC  SYN, (8)215470.40            ! line 22 SIC -- BIT-EXACT; landed pp.116/179
SCOMM   SYN, (8)215470.0             ! line 23 B; half word only; landed pp.116/179
JINSM   SYN, (8)221701.0             ! line 24 blank-operation half word -- BIT-EXACT (sweep above).
                                     !   p.195 OCR defines it at 221701.00
KUNRR   SYN, (8)221325.40            ! line 26 SIC -- BIT-EXACT; landed value
KKLOOP  SYN, (8)221321.40            ! line 27 B prints 221321.50; half word only; landed value
JRDLK   SYN, (8)221722.0             ! line 29 LX; half word only.  p.195 OCR defines it at 221722.00
JERRD   SYN, (8)221661.40            ! line 36 B prints 221661.50 so bit 32 IS checked; glyph call (1)
JLABIN  SYN, (8)221724.00            ! line 37 LF is a VFL operand -- BIT-EXACT.  p.195 OCR: "JLABIN XW ... LABEL SLOT"
SSCRPM  SYN(BU,64), 6.0              ! landed p.101 line 20 "-SCRATCH PAD MEMORY"; line 38 prints 000006.00
JBDLAB  SYN, (8)221664.40            ! line 39 BZAE prints 221664.76 so bit 32 IS checked; glyph call (1)
JBSPX   SYN, (8)221520.40            ! line 42 SIC -- BIT-EXACT; printed p.192 DEFINES it at 221520.40
JBSPE   SYN, (8)221514.0             ! line 43 B prints 221514.10; half word only; landed value
JERGK   SYN, (8)221725.0             ! line 44 LX; half word only.  p.195 OCR defines it at 221725.00

! ----- THE PAGE -------------------------------------------------
        SLC, (8)221617.0             ! NOT PRINTED.  CHECKED by the merge; see THE ORIGIN
JNEWXR  DRZ(N),(3)                   ! line  1 * -- THREE WORDS OF ZEROS; the Z is read off the ink
! lines 2-7 are comment cards: "*****ANALYSIS OF I/O INDICATORS FOR
! WRITE LABEL*****" and "LINKAGE....SIC,JWRITX...B,JWRITL".
JWRITL  TI,3,$1,JPREVX               ! line  8   printed name "J WRITL" (blank REFUSED by strap_asm)
        SIC,KCONVR                   ! line  9   -SET UP CHANNEL AND
        B,KCONV                      ! line 10   -UNIT NO.
        VF,JINSCU                    ! line 11   25-bit value field; rounds the counter to 221624.40
