! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! THE CHECKS
! ---------------------------------------------------------------
! FORTY-TWO of the forty-three located rows carry a !CHECK; line 1,
! the reservation, cannot be checked at all (see below).  Every
! label the page defines carries a !SYM.

!SYM JNEWXR 221617.00
!SYM JWRITL 221622.00
!SYM JEPGKF 221626.40
!SYM JUNRL  221634.40
!SYM JRDLAB 221636.00
!SYM JRWRIT 221644.40
!SYM JBACKT 221645.00
!SYM JTRYLG 221646.00
!
! LINE 1 CARRIES NO !CHECK, AND THAT IS NOT AN OVERSIGHT.  Its
! !SYM pins the location.  Its printed BINARY OUTPUT, 000003.00, is
! the reservation's COUNT, and `listing_oracle.render` has no way to
! produce a count: it renders the STORAGE at the location, which for
! a DRZ is the planted zero word and for a DR is nothing.  Measured:
!
!     statement         render('221617.00')   printed
!     DR(N),(3)         '000000.00 00'        000003.00
!     DRZ(N),(3)        '000000.00 00'        000003.00
!     DR(BU,64),(50)    '000000.00 00'        000062.00
!     DRZ(BU,64),(50)   '000000.00 00'        000062.00
!
! so a reservation row is UNCHECKABLE in both flavours, not merely
! Z-blind.  The landed decks already observe this (printed p.84's
! DRZ(BU,64),(50) carries no !CHECK; another deck says "Line 24's
! DRZ carries none").  >>> BUT docs/transcription_workflow.md STEP
! 3a STILL PRINTS "("004654.00", "000062.00", "line 5 T UNATB
! DRZ(BU,64),(50)")" AS ITS WORKED EXAMPLE OF A ROWS ENTRY, <<< and
! that row cannot pass; p.84's own deck does not contain it.  A
! transcriber who copies the example gets one red row on an
! otherwise correct page.  Reported rather than edited -- this deck
! may not write under docs/.
!
! What bounds the loss here: the count is pinned by ARITHMETIC
! instead.  Three words from 221617.00 is 221622.00, which is what
! line 8 PRINTS and what this deck's JWRITL !SYM checks; a count of
! 2 or 4 would move every one of the other forty-two rows.  So the
! COUNT is checked transitively and only the Z rests on ink.
!CHECK 221622.00 | 000021.00 80 221730.06 A0 | line 8 J WRITL TI,3,$1,JPREVX -- $1's cell is word 0o21, the first half; JPREVX is read off the second half to the HALF WORD only (.06 is the TI operation's own bits).  Printed name has a blank strap_asm cannot take
!CHECK 221623.00 | 221350.00 80 | line 9 SIC,KCONVR -SET UP CHANNEL AND -- a SIC reads every bit, so this CHECKS the landed KCONVR at 221350.00
!CHECK 221623.40 | 221335.10 00 | line 10 B,KCONV -UNIT NO. -- 0o00 OR 0o10; the half word is checked, the low bits are convention
!CHECK 221624.00 | 221704.20+ | line 11 VF,JINSCU -- a VF deposits the VALUE, all 24 bits plus sign, so bit 0o20 is a READING of JINSCU and not a convention.  25 bits, so the counter rounds to 221624.40 for line 12
!CHECK 221624.40 | 000001.11 8D 221626.74 02 | line 12 BB,SIOIND($13),JEPGKF -IF EPGK -- BB's first operand is a 24-bit BIT address, so SIOIND's bit 9 (0o11) is checked outright; 8D's low nibble is index $13; the branch half carries JEPGKF (this page's line 14 at 221626.40, hence 0o74 = 0o40 OR the BB code 0o34)
!CHECK 221625.40 | 000001.12 8D 221644.74 02 | line 13 BB,SIOIND+.1($13),JRWRIT -- bit 10 = 0o12, one bit on from line 12, which checks the bare-decimal ".1" conversion; JRWRIT is this page's line 41 at 221644.40
!CHECK 221626.40 | 221721.00 10 | line 14 JEPGKF LX,$0,JUNLDK -UNLOAD THE UNIT -- an index operation shows bit 32 only; byte 10 is LX
!CHECK 221627.00 | 221512.40 80 | line 15 SIC,KKRET -- SIC, so the landed KKRET at 221512.40 is CHECKED to the bit
!CHECK 221627.40 | 221505.10 00 | line 16 B,KIOREJ -- half word only
!CHECK 221630.00 | 221631.03 01 | line 17 LVI,$1,$+1.0 -- $ is 221630.00 so $+1.0 is 221631.00, a REAL address check; .03 is 2J+1 for J=1
!CHECK 221630.40 | 221525.10 00 | line 18 B,JSEOPT -- JSEOPT is printed p.192's line 27 at 221525.00
!CHECK 221631.00 | 000000.30 00 | line 19 NOP
!CHECK 221631.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 20 NOP
!CHECK 221632.00 | 221626.50 00 | line 21 B,JEPGKF -- JEPGKF is this page's line 14 at 221626.40: 0o40 OR 0o10 = 0o50, so this pins the label
!CHECK 221632.40 | 215470.40 80 | line 22 SIC,SCOMIC -INSTRUCT OPERATOR TO -- SIC, so the landed SCOMIC at 215470.40 is CHECKED
!CHECK 221633.00 | 215470.10 00 | line 23 B,SCOMM -PUT A RING IN REEL -- SCOMM and SCOMIC are the SAME WORD, half 0 and half 1, which is what the two rows together show
!CHECK 221633.40 | 221701.00 80 | line 24 ,JINSM -- a BLANK OPERATION FIELD, printed exactly so.  Measured to be in the bit-exact tier, so this row pins JINSM to 221701.00
!CHECK 221634.00 | 000010.00 80 | line 25 ,8.0 -- the same blank-operation form with a literal; 0o10 is word 8.  Two cards of parameters for the SCOMM call above
!CHECK 221634.40 | 221325.40 80 | line 26 JUNRL SIC,KUNRR -WAIT FOR UNIT TO -- SIC, so the landed KUNRR at 221325.40 is CHECKED
!CHECK 221635.00 | 221321.50 00 | line 27 B,KKLOOP -BECOME READY -- location carries the second asterisk; 0o40 OR 0o10 = 0o50 puts KKLOOP at 221321.40
!CHECK 221635.40 | 000003.07 02 | line 28 LCI,$3,3 -SET RD LABEL TALLY -- the address field is the VALUE 3, not an address; .07 is 2J+1 for J=3 and 02 is the LCI byte.  An LCI reads NOTHING below the word of its operand (printed p.190), but here the operand is a literal
!CHECK 221636.00 | 221722.00 10 | line 29 JRDLAB LX,$0,JRDLK -READ COMMAND -- half word only; printed p.195's OCR defines JRDLK at 221722.00 with "RD(SEOP),0.0($14),$+1.0 -READ LABEL COMMAND"
!CHECK 221636.40 | 221512.40 80 | line 30 SIC,KKRET -READ LABEL -- the same card as line 15, printed a second time
!CHECK 221637.00 | 221505.10 00 | line 31 B,KIOREJ -- the same card as line 16
!CHECK 221637.40 | 221640.43 01 | line 32 LVI,$1,$+1.0 - WAIT FOR TERMINATION -- $ is 221637.40 so $+1.0 is 221640.40 and 0o43 is 0o40 (bit 32) OR 2J+1 = 3.  The SAME statement as line 17 printing a DIFFERENT word, which is what makes the pair a check of the $ arithmetic
!CHECK 221640.00 | 221525.10 00 | line 33 B,JSEOPT
!CHECK 221640.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 34 NOP
!CHECK 221641.00 | 000000.30 00 | line 35 NOP
!CHECK 221641.40 | 221661.50 00 | line 36 B,JERRD -- 0o40 OR 0o10 = 0o50 puts JERRD at 221661.40; the final glyph is a D, glyph call (1)
!CHECK 221642.00 | 221724.00 80 036000.06 70 | line 37 LF(BU,30),JLABIN -IS THIS THE SAME LABEL -- a VFL OPERAND, so JLABIN is read to the bit; the second half carries length 0o36 = 30 and the LF byte 70
!CHECK 221643.00 | 000006.00 8C 036000.23 10 | line 38 KF(BU,30),SSCRPM($12) -- the landed SSCRPM at 000006.00, read bit-exactly by a VFL operand, indexed $12 (8C's low nibble); the second half is the SAME length 0o36 as line 37 with a DIFFERENT low field (.23 against .06), so the two rows together exercise the VFL second-half encoding
!CHECK 221644.00 | 221664.76 C0 | line 39 BZAE,JBDLAB -IF NOT SZME LABEL -- 0o76 is 0o40 (bit 32, so JBDLAB is at 221664.40) OR the branch code 0o36; C0 is the INFIX-Z byte the workflow records for BZAE against BAE's C2
!CHECK 221644.40 | 000003.07 02 | line 41 JRWRIT LCI,$3,3 -PREPARE TO REWRITE LABEL -- the same card as line 28, printed a second time; printed p.190 SYNs JRWRIT at this exact location
!CHECK 221645.00 | 221520.40 80 | line 42 JBACKT SIC,JBSPX -BSP THE TAPE -- SIC, so printed p.192's JBSPX at 221520.40 is CHECKED to the bit
!CHECK 221645.40 | 221514.10 00 | line 43 B,JBSPE -- half word only; agrees with the landed 221514.0
!CHECK 221646.00 | 221725.00 10 | line 44 JTRYLG LX,$0,JERGK -ERASE LONG GAP -- half word only.  printed p.195 line 1 branches to JTRYLG and prints 221646.10, which pins THIS label from the next page
!CHECK 221646.40 | 221512.40 80 | line 45 SIC,KKRET
!CHECK 221647.00 | 221505.10 00 | line 46 B,KIOREJ
!CHECK 221647.40 | 221650.43 01 | line 47 LVI,$1,$+1.0 -- $+1.0 from 221647.40 is 221650.40, so 0o43 again; the third printing of this card on the page and the second at a .40 origin
!CHECK 221650.00 | 221525.10 00 | line 48 B,JSEOPT
!CHECK 221650.40 | 000000.30 00 | line 49 NOP -- location carries the second asterisk, and lines 19/20/34/35/50 are the same statement WITHOUT it
!CHECK 221651.00 | 000000.30 00 | line 50 NOP -- the last row of the page; the counter leaves at 221651.40, which printed p.195 line 1 prints
